---
// /privacy — plain-language privacy policy covering what the site actually
// does: GA4 behind consent, Meta pixel on /lp/* only, Formspree, Calendly.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — The Linova Group"
  description="What The Linova Group collects, why, and the choices you have — in plain language."
  noindex={false}
>
  <div class="bg-film text-navy" data-ground="film">
    <article class="mx-auto max-w-[680px] px-6 pb-24 pt-24">
      <p class="label-caps !text-gold-deep">privacy</p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 font-display text-title">What we collect, and why</h1>
      <p class="label-caps mt-4 normal-case tracking-normal !text-gold-deep">last updated august 2026</p>

      <div class="mt-10 flex flex-col gap-5 text-body">
        <p>
          The Linova Group is a Canadian studio and follows PIPEDA
          (Canada's federal privacy law) and the spirit of Quebec's Law 25.
          Short version: nothing on this site tracks you until you say it can,
          and everything you send us is used to reply to you — not to build a
          profile of you.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-4 font-display text-heading">Analytics and ads</h2>
        <p>
          We use Google Analytics 4 to see which pages work. Ad and analytics
          cookies are <strong class="font-medium">off by default</strong> and
          turn on only if you choose "Allow analytics &amp; ads" in the banner.
          Decline and the site works exactly the same. Our ad landing pages
          (the ones you reach from a Facebook or Instagram ad) also use Meta's
          pixel and conversions tools so we know an ad led to a message —
          contact details sent that way are hashed before they leave our
          server.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-4 font-display text-heading">Forms and bookings</h2>
        <p>
          The contact form is processed by Formspree; what you type goes to
          our inbox and nowhere else. Call bookings run on Calendly, which has
          its own privacy policy; we receive the name, email, and time you
          give it.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-4 font-display text-heading">Your choices</h2>
        <p>
          You can decline cookies in the banner, clear your browser's storage
          to reset the choice, and ask us at any time what we hold about you
          or ask us to delete it. Use the{' '}
          <a href="/contact" class="text-navy underline decoration-gold decoration-2 underline-offset-4">contact form</a>
          — a person reads it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
